   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "What it expresses",
     "texto": [
      "The passive puts in the foreground what receives the action or the result, and often leaves out who did it: 문을 **열어요** = I open the door; 문이 **열려요** = the door opens / is open (depending on context). Not all forms describe something that happens «on its own»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Common forms",
     "texto": [
      "Some verbs form a passive with **-이-, -히-, -리-** or **-기-**: 열다 → **열리다**, 닫다 → **닫히다**, 잡다 → **잡히다**, 듣다 → **들리다**. The suffix cannot be safely deduced: learn each pair and its use. Other verbs have their own lexical passive form."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
